{"id":"st309","designation":"ST 309","title":"Transmission of Date and Time Zone Information in Binary Groups of Time and Control Code","state":"stabilized","suite":null,"official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st309/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st309/","checked_at":"2026-11-18"},"scope":"This standard specifies a coding technique for the transmission of date and time zone information in the user groups of a time and control code signal. A two-digit hexadecimal code in a pair of binary groups specifies the time zone and the format for the date encoding in the remaining six binary groups. Date information is encoded either as six decimal digits to display the date in the YYMMDD format or as six decimal digits in the modified Julian date (MJD) format.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"1","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"1 Scope","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"2 Conformance Notation","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"3 Normative References","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"4 Glossary","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"5 Date and Time Zone in Binary Groups","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"1.1","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"5.1 Time Zone, Date Format and Daylight Saving Time in Binary Groups 7 and 8","page":4},{"level":3,"title":"5.1.1 MJD format flag bit","page":4},{"level":3,"title":"5.1.2 Daylight Saving Time (DST) flag bit","page":5},{"level":3,"title":"5.1.3 Time zone coding","page":5},{"level":3,"title":"1.1.1","page":6},{"level":3,"title":"1.1.1","page":6},{"level":3,"title":"5.1.4 Binary group flags","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"5.2 Date as Binary Coded Decimal Digits","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"5.3 Modified Julian Date","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"5.4 Time and Date Coordination","page":6},{"level":1,"title":"Annex A Differences between GPS Time and UTC Time (Informative)","page":8},{"level":1,"title":"Annex A","page":9},{"level":1,"title":"Annex A","page":9},{"level":1,"title":"Annex B Additional Data in Binary Groups (Informative)","page":9},{"lev